Package: WolfPackR
Title: Identifies wolf packs based on genetic and spatial data
Version: 1.1.1
Authors@R: 
    person("Etienne", "Boncourt", , "etienne.boncourt@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8233-0190"))
Description: Identifies wolf packs, and the status of each individual, from pairwise relatedness and the locations of non-invasive genetic samples. Families are found by community detection on the relatedness graph; the space use of each individual is estimated by kernel density on a common grid; each individual is then assigned to the territory where its samples fall and gets a status (resident, putative or dated disperser, unrelated resident, transient, undetermined); families spread over several territories are split into spatially coherent packs. Also provides relatedness estimators (Queller & Goodnight, Lynch & Ritland, likelihood ratio), overlap indices, territory isopleths, pack summaries with permutation tests, interactive maps, follow-up through sampling periods, and tools to compare and assess the robustness of pack assignments. Built on igraph, sf and leaflet.
